CREOracleRecovery
├── A guard can directly apply the latest authenticated rejected report
│   ├── Recovery updates valuation without another forwarder delivery
│   ├── Unseen reports cannot be approved
│   ├── Malformed bytes and changes to any cached report field cannot authorize recovery
│   ├── A newer valid report replaces the candidate while the oracle remains frozen
│   └── Invalid destinations and snapshots cannot replace the cached candidate
├── Clearing recovery state does not change accounting
│   ├── Empty unfreeze clears the cache and retains the previous valuation and snapshot
│   ├── Manual freeze and workflow cutover invalidate the cached candidate
│   └── Delayed review does not consume the next reporting interval
└── Direct recovery retains all non-movement checks
    ├── Delivery age is checked again, including its exact maximum boundary
    ├── Immutable NAV age is checked again and failed review preserves the candidate
    └── Insufficient liquidity does not freeze valuation and later cash waits for its covering report
